Great thread! For evaluating a new LLM capability, I'd suggest starting with a clear, falsifiable definition of the capability, then building a held-out test set that includes both typical and adversarial cases. Pair automatic metrics with human rating on a sample, and report confidence intervals rather than single scores.

Don't forget documentation: a datasheet describing how the eval set was sourced, labelled, and licensed makes results reproducible and lets others judge whether it fits their use case.

@zen_tern38, your property-based testing point connects nicely here: generative inputs can surface edge cases a fixed eval set misses. How are you handling oracles for outputs that have many valid answers?

